From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:47:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 117/118] netifd: packet steering: leave a disabled service
 alone

rc.common's reload() runs reload_service whether the service is
enabled or not, while the interface trigger exists only for a running
service. So the hotplug script that steers a wireless interface made
after boot would steer it even after "/etc/init.d/packet_steering
disable". Exit unless the service is enabled, as the review of the
upstream pull request asked. Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/network/config/netifd/Makefile                          | 2 +-
 .../config/netifd/files/etc/hotplug.d/net/20-packet-steering    | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile b/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile
index 40c1ffafce4..4a4a709d6fb 100644
--- a/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=netifd
-PKG_RELEASE:=5
+PKG_RELEASE:=6
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=$(PROJECT_GIT)/project/netifd.git
diff --git a/package/network/config/netifd/files/etc/hotplug.d/net/20-packet-steering b/package/network/config/netifd/files/etc/hotplug.d/net/20-packet-steering
index 32f391381be..08bbdc0e46f 100644
--- a/package/network/config/netifd/files/etc/hotplug.d/net/20-packet-steering
+++ b/package/network/config/netifd/files/etc/hotplug.d/net/20-packet-steering
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 
 [ "$ACTION" = add ] && [ "$DEVTYPE" = wlan ] || exit 0
 [ -x /etc/init.d/packet_steering ] || exit 0
+/etc/init.d/packet_steering enabled || exit 0
 
 PENDING=/var/run/packet-steering.pending
 [ -e "$PENDING" ] && exit 0
-- 
2.43.0

